From: Saha Developers <dev@saha-project.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: lemans-evk: fix PSCI reset arguments

The reboot-mode based PSCI driver consumes <reset-type, cookie>, unlike
the older vendor reset implementation's <cookie, reset-type>. The EVK
retains the old order, passing type 0 / cookie 1 for EDL and hanging
after shutdown instead of enumerating the download interface.

Keep the firmware values but encode them in the order documented by
Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/psci.yaml. Limit the override to
this EVK; the other Lemans boards need their own hardware validation.

Upstream-Status: Pending [IQ-9075 hardware bring-up on pinned qcom-6.18.y]
Signed-off-by: Saha Developers <dev@saha-project.local>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/lemans-evk.dts | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/lemans-evk.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/lemans-evk.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/lemans-evk.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/lemans-evk.dts
@@ -913,8 +913,8 @@
 
 &psci {
 	reboot-mode {
-		mode-bootloader = <0x10001 0x2>;
-		mode-edl = <0 0x1>;
+		mode-bootloader = <0x2 0x10001>;
+		mode-edl = <0x1 0>;
 	};
 };
 
